.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-LIST-BUCKETS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-list-buckets \- list storage buckets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm list-buckets
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-p\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-direction\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fIDIRECTION\fR]
[\fB\-\-include\-internal\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists storage buckets, optionally filtered by name prefix and
paginated.
.PP
Euclid's own buckets are left out. The bucket applications are deployed
from is one of them \- EAP creates it when it starts \- so
.B \-\-include\-internal
is how it is seen. Hidden is all that means: the bucket is read and
written by name like any other.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only list buckets whose name starts with this prefix. Optional; if
omitted, all buckets are listed.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of buckets to return. Defaults to \fI-1\fR (no paging).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index to return when \fB\-\-page\-size\fR is set.
Defaults to \fI-1\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sort\-column " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Column to sort results by. Defaults to \fIname\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-sort\-direction " " \fIDIRECTION\fR
\fIasc\fR or \fIdesc\fR. Defaults to \fIasc\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-internal
Also list euclid's own buckets. Honoured for administrators only, and
ignored for anybody else rather than refused.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The matching buckets are printed as JSON (possibly an empty list).
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or the
server rejected the request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm list-buckets

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm list-buckets \e
    --prefix report- --page-size 20 --page-index 0 --sort-column name

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm list-buckets \e
    --include-internal
.fi
.RE
